  "releaseVerdict": "Passed the exercised Java tax-advisor (131 methods), TypeScript TaxAdvisor (329 methods), TWE, and EITC tests. Redis emulator contracts, Redis-backed graph reconstruction, packaged MCP runtime and application-restart restoration passed. Real Redis infrastructure qualification remains separate. Existing consumer navigation/display/link limitations remain. Direct File backend functional qualification remains incomplete; legacy frontend and unmodified saved returns are not drop-in compatible.",
  "applicationJavascriptLimitations": [
    "Chrome smoke run covers synthetic default English multi-question scenarios. Other locales, mobile layouts, PDF generation, optional single-question mode, and exhaustive browser suites were not exercised.",
    "Session comparisons cover synthetic scenarios, not every saved session or tax calculation. Root-result comparisons include incomplete/provisional values and the recorded unchanged TWE error.",
    "Existing wildcard display code reads private Scala.js vector fields and truncates to 32 items. Full optimization also breaks private field access and currency detection; reproduced with HEAD baseline. App Makefiles currently copy fastLinkJS.",
    "Typed Boolean writes persist correctly but return a Scala tuple without the string setter errorType/warnings DTO. This predates candidate. No current MultiEnum declarations were found in these dictionaries; their generic UI handlers were not exercised.",
    "Chrome confirmed that both applications permit Next while a rejected replacement is visible, using the prior accepted graph value. Returning/reloading restores the accepted value. Existing navigation handlers inspect completeness without gating the active field error.",
    "EITC results-page income edit links target /app/eitc/income/ and return 404; generated income page is /app/eitc/agi/. Existing flow XML hardcodes those destinations.",
    "Existing handlers ignore the new warnings field. Introducing Warn limits requires consumer warning UI; the current dictionaries do not exercise that feature."
  ],
  "redisQualificationLimits": [
    "Mocks qualify exercised application Redis commands and state contracts, not production Redis infrastructure.",
    "Application restart restoration was tested while the mock Redis process remained running. Redis server restart durability, eviction, TLS/auth, failover and cluster routing were not tested.",
    "The ioredis-mock JSON shim is not lua-cjson parity. Generated intake revisions cover 0..1000000 and budget units 1..1000; exact large-number formatting and TTL rounding require real Redis comparison.",
    "Source-review gaps recorded in app docs include concurrent deletion during message persistence, fractional rate-limit additions, Java long-version precision, and delete/recreate ABA with reused IDs. No claim of those properties passing is made."
  ]
